---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PartnerImage from '@/components/PartnerImage.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="L2 Data Architecture | Arkansas Campaign Data Cooperative" description="Deep dive into L2 voter file fields, contact intelligence, districts, wealth, donors, HaystaqDNA models—and how the Arkansas cooperative uses them.">
<section class="page-hero">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / L2 Data</p>
        <p class="brand-lockup">Enhanced statewide intelligence · <a class="brand-link" href="https://l2-data.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">L2 Data</a></p>
        <h1 transition:name="page-title">Hundreds of fields. One cooperative purchase.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">For over 50 years, L2 has been the gold standard for voter contact and targeting information. If the cooperative funds acquisition, Arkansas participants receive jurisdiction-appropriate access to this enhanced architecture—subject to final licensing.</p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/cooperative/">Contribution minimums</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/assets/L2-Voter-Data-Dictionary.pdf">Data dictionary PDF</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://l2-data.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Visit L2</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <nav class="page-toc" aria-label="On this page">
          <strong>On this page</strong>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#scale">National scale</a></li>
            <li><a href="#dictionary">Voter file taxonomy</a></li>
            <li><a href="#contact">Contact &amp; location</a></li>
            <li><a href="#models">Predictive layer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#workflow">L2 workflow</a></li>
            <li><a href="#arkansas">Arkansas cooperative use</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>
        <div class="partner-band">
          <PartnerImage variant="l2-logo" loading="lazy" />
          <p>Field names and product claims summarize L2’s public data dictionary and marketing. Authoritative detail: <a href="https://l2-data.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">l2-data.com</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="scale" class="section section-problem">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 >National scale, Arkansas application</h2>
        <div class="stats-row">
          <div class="stat-block"><p class="stat-num">217M+</p><p class="stat-label">Voter records (national)</p></div>
          <div class="stat-block"><p class="stat-num">260M+</p><p class="stat-label">Consumer records</p></div>
          <div class="stat-block"><p class="stat-num">~1.6M</p><p class="stat-label">Arkansas cooperative target file</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="stats-row">
          <div class="stat-block"><p class="stat-num">800+</p><p class="stat-label">Consumer attributes</p></div>
          <div class="stat-block"><p class="stat-num">400</p><p class="stat-label">Demographic fields</p></div>
          <div class="stat-block"><p class="stat-num">160+</p><p class="stat-label">HaystaqDNA models</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="lead">L2 aggregates sources into a web-based ecosystem for selecting, analyzing, and micro-targeting—no desktop install required.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="dictionary" class="section section-foundation">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 >Voter file taxonomy</h2>
        <p class="lead">From L2’s voter data dictionary—hundreds of fields to find target voters:</p>
        <div class="taxonomy-grid">
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Identity &amp; registration</h3>
            <p>LALVOTERID, state/county IDs, name, gender, age, birth date confidence, place of birth, veteran, active/inactive, registration dates, party &amp; party switcher, progressive/moderate/conservative flags.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Contact &amp; location</h3>
            <p>Cell, landline, residence &amp; mailing addresses with CASS codes, lat/long accuracy, Do Not Call, walk-list zig-zag/odd-even, time zone, urbanicity, population density.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Districts</h3>
            <p>County, precinct, U.S. House, state house/senate, municipalities, school/college/judicial/special districts, fire/hospital/police, utility, flood, and more.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Household demographics</h3>
            <p>Head of household, religion, marital status, adults/children counts, disabled/senior/young adult flags, household parties, ethnic coding, language proficiency.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Voting history</h3>
            <p>All election levels, frequency, early/absentee history, performance, absentee type—plus mover history across districts and prior performance.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Wealth &amp; finance</h3>
            <p>Income, net worth, credit rating (modeled), CRA class, credit cards, investor flags, FEC donor history and amounts.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Property &amp; housing</h3>
            <p>Purchase year/price, estimated &amp; assessed value, mortgage, dwelling type, square footage, bedrooms, pool, owner flags.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Donors &amp; philanthropy</h3>
            <p>Charitable, political, religious, environmental, health, arts, and cause-specific donor indicators.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Lifestyle &amp; interests</h3>
            <p>Sports, travel, food, apparel, media consumption, DIY, tech early adopter, upscale/common living groups.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Automotive</h3>
            <p>In-market car, make/model/year, motorcycle make/model, work spender flags.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Census &amp; statistical areas</h3>
            <p>DMA, tract/block group/block, CSA/CBSA/MSA, area % children/married/Spanish-speaking, median income &amp; education, social ranking indices.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="taxonomy-card">
            <h3>Digital identifiers</h3>
            <p>MAID (mobile ad ID), IP, and verified emails (highly cleaned; often purchased separately from standard taxonomy).</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-links">
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/assets/L2-Voter-Data-Dictionary.pdf">Full L2 voter data dictionary (PDF)</a>
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://l2-data.com/voter-data/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">L2 voter data product</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="contact" class="section section-platform">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 >Every touchpoint</h2>
        <p class="lead">L2 positions contact lists for the channels campaigns actually run:</p>
        <ul class="feature-list two-col">
          <li>Phone lists</li>
          <li>Email lists</li>
          <li>Text lists</li>
          <li>Mailing lists</li>
          <li>Canvassing / walking lists</li>
          <li>Digital targeting</li>
        </ul>
        <p>That directly addresses Arkansas’ operational pain: missing mobiles, incomplete emails, and stale addresses. <a href="/problem/">See the problem brief →</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="models" class="section">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 >Predictive layer</h2>
        <div class="drill-grid">
          <article class="drill-card">
            <h3>HaystaqDNA models</h3>
            <p>Hundreds of issue, behavior, and candidate flags/scores (0–100) beyond the standard L2 taxonomy. <a href="/models/">Open models brief →</a></p>
          </article>
          <article class="drill-card">
            <h3>Causeway viewership models</h3>
            <p>L2 also references viewership &amp; issue models (e.g., streaming platforms) for additional targeting dimensions.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="drill-card">
            <h3>Verified emails</h3>
            <p>Highly cleaned, up-to-date emails for direct outreach and identity resolution / digital matching.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="drill-card">
            <h3>National consumer database</h3>
            <p>All-adults consumer insights for DTC marketing, research, and analytics layered onto voter universes.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/assets/L2-Haystaq-Model-List.pdf">Haystaq model list PDF</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="workflow" class="section section-problem">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 >Using L2 data</h2>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li><strong>Define your universe</strong> Filters across demographic, voter, consumer, and modeled behaviors.</li>
          <li><strong>Pull counts and analyze</strong> Compare criteria across districts; view geographically.</li>
          <li><strong>Solidify selection</strong> Mapping to cut turf and confirm counts.</li>
          <li><strong>Export records</strong> Excel, CSV, or DBF—then engage via Electd, VAN, or managed programs.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="source-links">
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://l2-data.com/datamapping/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">L2 DataMapping</a>
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://l2-data.com/data-hygiene/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Data hygiene</a>
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://l2-data.com/states/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">State voter records</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="arkansas" class="section section-foundation">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 >Arkansas cooperative use</h2>
        <p class="lead">We are working to acquire a professionally enhanced Arkansas voter and consumer file (~1.6 million records) through L2, funded by cooperative minimums—not by any single campaign alone.</p>
        <div class="policy-callout">
          <h3>Contribution minimums apply</h3>
          <p>Published cooperative amounts are <strong>minimums</strong>. If you can contribute more, please do. Local races in metro areas of <strong>50,000+</strong> pay the <strong>county minimum ($300)</strong>.</p>
          <p><a href="/cooperative/#minimums">Read full policy →</a></p>
        </div>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>Improve phones, emails, and addresses feeding <a href="/platform/">Electd</a> and <a href="/van/">VAN</a></li>
          <li>Apply Haystaq scores for persuasion, turnout, and channel strategy</li>
          <li>Keep campaign-owned contacts firewalled — <a href="/privacy/">privacy</a></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="source-links">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/join/?intent=reserve">Reserve cooperative pricing</a>
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://l2-data.com/contact-us/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Contact L2</a>
        </div>
        <p class="attr-note">L2 product names, statistics, field taxonomy, and imagery © <a href="https://l2-data.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">L2, Inc.</a> Arkansas Campaign Data Cooperative packages cooperative purchasing for Arkansas participants.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

</BaseLayout>

